description: Re-measure how much slower the llvm driver compiles than the GC driver, now that the runtime library is cached per program, to size the function cache work (plans 2 and 3).
 
 The last numbers are from 2026-10-09: 20.3 s against 1.34 s for (println 1), 12.4 s of it re-analysing the runtime. The measurement becomes a workflow.mk target, so a later run uses the same command.
 
 Measurements that close it, each with its conditions (revision, load average, run count, through checks/quiet.sh):
 
 - M1 compile time per program for both drivers over a fixed set: a one-line program, corpus/scalar/fib.clj, and one legmacs-sized program; median of 5.
 - M2 for the llvm driver, the split between runtime analysis and the program's own lowering.
 - M3 the ratio of M1's llvm and GC medians, stated as a bound (llvm/GC <= r) under M1's conditions.
